  <meiHead>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Transcription: Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document NY 905-II-0192-6TR, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/b4386715-8f1b-4d90-ade9-42767952a65b/NY%20905-II-0192-6TR.xml, made with OMMR4all according to Corpus Monodicum's record, corrected against the facsimile for eChant (see corpus-monodicum-corrected/corrections.md); © Corpus Monodicum. Pitches at the manuscript's level, a fifth above the Graduale Synopticum witnesses, and an octave lower than the file. Neume division, shapes and facsimile zones: a close reading of f. 192r on the Geese Book site's Zoomify image (October 2026), written as Gothic (Hufnagel) neumes on the manuscript's five-line staff with its C clef.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">US-NYpm</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">MS M.905, vol. II</idno>
            <ptr target="https://www.themorgan.org/manuscript/159920"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Gradual in two volumes for St. Lorenz, Nuremberg (the "Geese Book"), written 1507–1510, vol. II dated 1510 (Morgan Library record); Gothic notation on five-line staves. Facsimile viewer: https://geesebook.asu.edu/browse.aspx%3Fv=2&amp;p=383&amp;l=english.html. The gradual for the Common of Virgins, ff. 192r–192v. Images: Corpus Monodicum (Würzburg IIIF).</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document NY 905-II-0192-6TR, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/b4386715-8f1b-4d90-ade9-42767952a65b/NY%20905-II-0192-6TR.xml (respond) and document NY 905-II-0192-11TR, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/df8b00fa-3fe6-4705-bae2-8c1e5e8290e0/NY%20905-II-0192-11TR.xml (verse), made with OMMR4all according to Corpus Monodicum's record, corrected against the facsimile for eChant (see corpus-monodicum-corrected/corrections.md). Pitches at the manuscript's level (a fifth above the Graduale Synopticum witnesses), an octave lower than the file.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
